                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I really like the concept, but the game is still very much in early alpha stage despite being a full release now.\n\nThe controls shown in game (lower right) don't match the actual controls in the settings, which of course is a huge cause of confusion. X is for fight mode, but nothing happens when pressing X. I tried every other key on the keyboard to try to attack or scare off the opponent, but my silverback would just stand there and take the beating. And I found no option to remap \"scare\" or \"attack\" in the Controls. Only \"attack mode\" itself can be remapped. Would be a bonus if it was possible to see the controls in the game without having to go to the main menu everytime you want to see what the controls are.\n\nThere are bugs like predators not attacking your silverback despite standing literally on top of a lion or a crocodile. At other times they would attack on sight.\n\nThe game wouldn't save my progress. Everytime I loaded a save, it would put me back to an earlier stage of the game.\n\nThe same key (C by default) is used for sleeping/bonding. I tried using said key when next to another gorilla, but my silverback would just sit down and that was it. I tried waiting but nothing happened with the bonding bar shown on the other gorilla. \n\nThe audio is completely wonky. The \"music\" option in the settings control things like bird sounds and the \"sound\" option didn't appear to do anything - not that one can hear, when in the menu anyway. When in the game sounds of the other animals were crazy loud when close to them despite of me having turned both the \"music\" and \"sound\" more than half way down.\n\nSomehow I got two achievements. \nFind Troop (Find all adult troop members): So there are only 2 adult troop members??? And you don't even have to go anywhere to find them, since they were within like 30 meters of where my silverback spawned in. Seemed pretty odd to not even have to go looking for them, since that is like the main part of the game (based on the description).\n\nMate with your troop(You managed to mate with a troop member): Erhm how? I wandered around near the other two gorillas that I saw and tried to bond (unsuccesfully to my knowledge) with one as mentioned above, but at no point did I see any indication of mating occuring in the game - not even with a little text notification.\n\nThere are other issues that I could list, but I will stop here. Overall I wish the devs would have stuck with the game and actually finished it properly, because it is a great concept, but there is no way that I can recommend it in its current state.",
